type: software
title: "The energy an isolated half of a critical chain cannot give up: conformal amplitudes, dispersion, and the cost of conserving particle number"
abstract: "Unrefereed research candidate. The bound energy of an isolated half of a critical chain (the energy that no unitary on the half can extract) obeys Q ~ 3v S^2/(2 pi c L) in a regulated boundary conformal field theory and in the open hopping and critical Ising chains; in a family of free-fermion chains sharing one critical ground state it scales as S^(m+1)/L^m, set by the flattest zero of the block dispersion, so the conjectured law of Mula et al. is not universal; in one range-three chain, unrestricted, number-conserving and one-body controls leave residuals of different orders."
